  Implementation parameters
    - Runtime metresPerWorldUnit=1; controlled submissions validate conversions within 1e-6..1e6.
      DDA visits at most 402 cells for the admitted <=200-square native grid. View/light subdivisions
      per occupied column default to 4/1 and are bounded to 1..16 / 1..4. Detail defaults to amplitude
      .15, inward softness 2 world units and approximately .08 noise cells/world unit. The periodic
      material lattice uses integer frequency over 12,800 world units for recenter/wind consistency.
      Detail-disabled transport uses exact constant-column extinction. Typed controls are present;
      reference/default and sample/detail settings exposure is recorded under Phase 5.
    - Directional phase is HG(g=.6); the extra octave uses isotropic phase with .5 contribution and
      .5 occlusion. Solar and lunar secondary rays share the view density. View transmission ends
      below 1e-6; light saturation accounts for both single and extra-octave transmission, including
      zero occlusion, without infinite optical depth. The pre-map source bound includes both phase
      peaks, environment/aerial/local fog and conservative FP32 interval-accumulation headroom.

