Phase 5 implementation and verification (2026-10-16)
  Task-to-document and implementation traceability
    - Reduced targets -> Proposal / Quality and temporal behavior, Ownership boundary;
      Phase 1 / OIT and temporal payload contract -> CloudVolumeSurface, CloudVolumeReconstruction,
      CloudTraceProgram and cloud_volume_trace.fsh. Ceil-half extents cover odd view dimensions.
      Each of three persistent sets holds FP32 RGB bin revealage, scalar overall revealage, RGBA
      glow metadata, three RGBA accumulations and RGBA first/last contributing depth plus native
      opaque/liquid depth. Replacement writes preserve neutral empty pixels; internal passes do
      not blend against or sample the live engine OIT targets. Pipelines/images persist between
      frames and are retired on resize/reload/disposal. The view is bounded to 16,384 per dimension
      and nominal total image allocation to 1 GiB before allocation. Nominal texel storage is
      288 bytes per reduced pixel across trace and two history sets; this is calculated allocation,
      not measured resident memory. Native producer and other resources are additional costs.
    - History/reprojection -> Proposal / Quality and temporal behavior, Publication and native
      lifecycle; Phase 1 / borrowed input and temporal payload -> CloudTemporalHistory,
      CloudTemporalParameters, CloudTemporalProgram and cloud_volume_temporal.fsh. Weak producer
      identity plus world/allocation/shader/content certificates, exact view extent/projection,
      camera cuts/frame continuity, calibration, settings, medium and completed light publication
      admit history. Native placement differences remove integer recentering and committed wind;
      residual wind already exists in placement. This matches the actual trace origin without
      adding a second camera/wind translation. Current inverse view and retained previous view-
      projection handle camera rotation. Rotating two-by-two phases select exact view pixels;
      phase-aware nearest history selection accounts for the prior phase and odd trailing tiles.
      Missing input, bypass, reload, resize and release withdraw history. No reflection view uses it.
      Native worker source confirms raw uploads on completed worker commits with a 40-ms sleep:
      upload identity must be monotonic, but a routine upload alone does not discard convergence.
      Current depth/support and optical-change rejection plus neighborhood bounds handle weather.
    - Reconstruction/composition -> Proposal / Scene integration, Density integration and lighting;
      Atmosphere.Publication / Atmospheric transport and Publication contract; Phase 1 / OIT and
      temporal payload -> CloudResolveProgram, cloud_volume_resolve.fsh and reduced physical history.
      Every accepted sample uses common weights for all six payload channels,
      including weighted alpha and attenuation. History radiance remains physical FP32; only final
      accumulated RGB receives the frozen scene encoding. No alpha/reveal/depth exposure or second
      premultiplication is applied. Shared integration keeps density, self-shadowing, one extra
      scattering octave and aerial/local fog identical to the direct reference. Full-view density-
      only validation checks current coverage, all bins and both native clips. Rejected pixels run
      the common exact reference integration, preserving thin columns and foreground/liquid edges.
      Final submission uses existing Reveal/Reveal/Glow/Add/Add/Add blending and native resolve.
      No new producer, atmosphere integration, native hook, reflection or cast-shadow path is added.
    - Controls -> Proposal / Quality and temporal behavior, Simple cloud rendering; parent
      BaselineShading / Scope and shared contracts -> CloudRenderingSettings, VgeConfig.Clouds,
      existing ConfigLib mappings and English labels. Clouds.FullResolutionReference defaults false;
      setting it true bypasses reduced tracing/history/upsampling and invalidates retained history.
      ViewSamples (1..16), LightSamples (1..4), Detail, DetailAmplitude (0..0.95), EdgeWidth (.01..10)
      and NoiseScale (.001..1) use identical immutable selections for reference/default and source
      admission before Opaque. Nonfinite persisted values restore bounded defaults. Simple has no
      dependency on these passes. Permanent architecture documentation remains the later cleanup task.
    - Verification -> Proposal / Acceptance and implementation qualification; Phase 5 / deterministic
      reference/reset comparison -> CloudTemporalHistoryTests and GPU/CloudVolumeReconstructionTests,
      alongside existing analytic CloudVolumeDrawTests and cloud/native/scene regressions. Tiny views
      exercise real owned shader binaries and native six-target blending. These comparisons measure
      reconstruction error against the same transport model; independent analytic transport checks
      remain separate. Live appearance, complete lifecycle qualification and measured performance
      remain later acceptance requirements.

  Implementation parameters and review
    - Temporal weight is .75, with one shared acceptance decision for the entire payload. First/last
      support compatibility allows max(2 world units, 2% representative distance), extent difference
      max(2 world units, 5% thickness), and native depth difference <=2e-5. Overall/bin transmission
      jumps >.05 reject history; previous channels are clamped to a compatible 3x3 current neighborhood.
      Invalid/nonfinite/negative previous channels reject the entire record. Static accepted history
      residual decays by .75 per update; it is bounded accumulation, not an unlimited previous layer.
    - Four-tap phase-aware upsampling compares reconstructed opaque/liquid foreground distances,
      with max(2 world units, 1% foreground distance) tolerance and shared bilateral weights for
      all six payload channels. Samples wholly in front of both clips can survive background-depth
      changes. Cloud intervals extending behind a new foreground clip are conservatively rejected.
      Rejected bilinear taps use the nearest depth-compatible payload in a bounded 3x3 reduced
      stencil; no compatible sample submits neutral OIT. Resolve never evaluates density/transport.
      Reduced sampling can miss narrow silhouettes and newly exposed partial cloud intervals.
      Full-resolution reference mode remains separate; live quality/performance gates stay open.
    - Reconstruction comparisons retain .021 attenuation and .045 normalized-payload tolerances
      outside the one-pixel full-resolution reference neighborhood envelope. Raw pointwise errors
      are recorded separately because spatial filtering is approximate. CPU/observable temporal probes
      use 1e-5 attenuation/alpha and 1e-4 accumulated-RGB tolerances. Measured residuals and final
      receipts are recorded below. No game launch or performance acceptance occurred.
