Reduced-resolution resolve correction (2026-10-16)
  - Default rendering keeps ceil-half width/height tracing and physical temporal reconstruction.
    CloudResolveProgram now has its own depth/history/scene-encoding bindings, with no cloud-map,
    density parameters or atmosphere textures. The unused visibility march include is removed.
  - Full-view resolve performs four-tap phase-aware depth filtering. Rejected bilinear taps may
    select one nearest depth-compatible payload from a bounded 3x3 reduced stencil. All six OIT
    channels use the same weights or selected record; no compatible record writes neutral OIT.
    No default resolve branch evaluates density, self-shadowing or complete transport. The explicit
    full-resolution reference remains available separately.
  - Comparison methodology distinguishes raw pointwise filtering error from error outside the
    one-pixel spatial reference envelope. Original .021 attenuation/.045 normalized-payload
    tolerances were used for that historical candidate and are retired. Authored zero-map payloads verify exact interpolation,
    shared channel weights, once-only physical RGB encoding and native Glow blending. Foreground
    occlusion, partial in-cloud disocclusion and recovery have explicit GPU regression coverage.
  - Final production and fixture SPIRV/C# builds passed. Combined cloud CPU, source, binding,
    registry and shader-selection checks passed 156/156, with no failed or skipped tests:
    VanillaGraphicsExpanded.Tests/TestResults/cloud-resolve-final-contracts.trx.
  - Final reconstruction/history checks passed 48/48, with no failed/skipped tests:
