Shared depth-hierarchy reuse (2026-10-16)
  - The PBR composition root supplies owned Volumetric cloud demand to the existing shared
    DepthHierarchyRenderer. Cloud-only demand produces the same single chain with AO/LumOn off;
    Simple/Off do not independently retain it. Clouds neither allocate nor rebuild a hierarchy.
  - CloudVolumeRenderer borrows only a valid matching frame/view/extent publication and forwards
    the same hierarchy texture to reduced tracing, full-resolution reference and spatial resolve.
    Missing or stale publication invalidates cloud history and skips submission.
  - sceneDepth now denotes the shared corrected material hierarchy. cloud_depth.glsl explicitly
    selects mip zero and combines it with independent primary visibility depth to preserve opaque-
    pass particle clipping. Liquid depth remains independent. Existing six-target OIT submission,
    physical storage, cloud density and lighting are unchanged.
  - This is shared-resource reuse only. Coarse HZB traversal, tile culling, min/max extensions and
    cloud-density acceleration are not implemented. Live appearance/performance gates remain open.
  - Verification: production/test builds passed; 154 CPU/source/catalog/registry/selection and
    78 unique GPU checks passed, zero skips. Initial cloud-hzb-focused.trx recorded 89/94 passed
    with five fixture/assertion failures: camera-world fixture shape and assumptions of zero
    foreground cloud while inside its volume. These were corrected in tests only. All five,
