Change-driven hierarchy enablement (2026-10-16)
  - Removed the optional additionalDemand callback and all per-frame consumer/settings eligibility
    evaluation from DepthHierarchyRenderer. It starts disabled and exposes cached Enabled state;
    SetEnabled changes allocation/publication lifetime only when the execution state transitions.
  - PbrModSystem owns DepthHierarchyEnablement. It captures SSAO quality once, registers its native
    settings watcher, and listens to the frozen LumOn generation and active actual volumetric
    ownership. Mode selection without functioning ownership does not request depth storage.
    Stable frame callbacks never reread settings or poll consumers for eligibility.
  - Cloud ownership emits notifications on actual activation/release, including teardown, rather
    than on each native mode check. The shader-mode event publishes a frozen non-null generation;
    queued configuration and asset-lifetime resets do not prematurely choose a new mode.
  - Disabling immediately withdraws publication/releases resources; reenabling allocates lazily.
    Resize, world teardown and shader reload retain their independent publication/resource hooks.
    Enabled frames still regenerate current scene depth once in Opaque and validate frame/view.
  - Installed engine inspection confirms DoPostProcessingEffects is a transient screen-pass gate:
    ScreenManager.Render writes false, then GuiScreenRunningGame.RenderToPrimary writes true
    before the world loop every frame. It is not frozen as a persistent eligibility setting and
    its setter is not hooked. Evidence: artifacts/DepthHierarchyEnablement/native-postprocessing-gate.txt.
  - Validation: isolated shader-enabled build passed (0 errors, existing repository analyzer
    warnings); 91/91 focused checks passed with no skips. Coverage includes native settings
    notifications, frozen mode changes, actual cloud activation/release, unchanged disabled
    frames without settings reads, unsubscribe/stale callbacks, immediate retirement/recreation,
    hierarchy lifecycle, cloud ownership/draw, composition shutdown, scene color and LumOn.
    Receipt: artifacts/DepthHierarchyEnablement/focused.trx; build.log and focused.log are siblings.
  - Native SSAO UI and preset changes use the watcher-enabled settings indexer; preset shader
    reload suppression does not silence settings notifications. No reload polling or extra native
    settings hook is required. Native inspection evidence is retained in the same artifact folder.
    No game launch/deployment or visual/performance qualification occurred.

Shared reactive enablement (2026-10-16)
  - PipelineEnablement now owns the shared native watchers, applied VGE configuration snapshot,
